# General Best Practices

## Git
- Conventional commits: `type(scope): message`
- Review `git status` + `git diff --stat` before committing
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, key vaults, `node_modules`, build artifacts
- No force-push or amend without explicit permission

## Config discipline
- One canonical file per infra fact; rules/docs LINK instead of copying
- Full absolute paths for interpreters on Windows; verify spawned servers start
- Idempotent setup + health check + watchdog for anything that must stay up

## Quality
- Fix warnings; don't suppress them. Lint/format before commit.
- Prefer explicit types; keep functions focused.
- Every behavioral change ships with verification (test, headless check, or measured before/after).
